4
00:00:04.914 --> 00:00:06.559 line:15%
Yes, the Tower of David Museum.

5
00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:07.459
Why don't you show me the different

6
00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:08.714
quarters in the city?

7
00:00:08.714 --> 00:00:10.241
[Eilat] This is the Christian Quarter.

8
00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:12.635
Christian Quarter over here.
This is the Muslim Quarter.

9
00:00:12.635 --> 00:00:13.772
Dome of the Rock, beautiful,

10
00:00:13.772 --> 00:00:15.370
Muslim Quarter.
This is the Jewish Quarter,

11
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.459
most of it you won't see,

12
00:00:16.459 --> 00:00:18.431
because it's down towards the valley.

13
00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:20.385
The Armenian Quarter is right there.

14
00:00:20.385 --> 00:00:21.656
The Armenians have a quarter?

15
00:00:21.656 --> 00:00:22.489
Armenians, yes.

16
00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.205
I don't understand why they get a quarter.

17
00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:26.733
Because they were here.
They got all of Glendale.

18
00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:28.637
This is my assistant, Sona, she's Armenian.

19
00:00:28.637 --> 00:00:29.520
Hi.
(laughter and applause)

20
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.749
Sona, did you know that the Armenians had a quarter?

21
00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:32.594
I did.

22
00:00:32.594 --> 00:00:33.427
Have you hung out in the quarter,

23
00:00:33.427 --> 00:00:35.092
have your family gone to the quarter a lot?

24
00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:35.925
No, nobody's gone.
No!

25
00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:37.673
You guys don't use it, right?

26
00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:38.830
No.
You guy are all hanging out

27
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.847
at Zankou Chicken in East Hollywood.

28
00:00:41.847 --> 00:00:42.689
(applause)

29
00:00:42.689 --> 00:00:43.522
What about the Catholics?

30
00:00:43.522 --> 00:00:45.013
A lot of Christians don't love-

31
00:00:45.013 --> 00:00:48.339
well, especially Irish Catholics, we're loud,

32
00:00:48.339 --> 00:00:50.156
we throw potatoes at each other.

33
00:00:50.156 --> 00:00:52.768
I promise you, you do not want the Irish Catholics in here.

34
00:00:52.768 --> 00:00:56.640
Cause there's gonna be Red Sox sports bars everywhere.

35
00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.556
Sounds good.

36
00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:58.954
No, you've been to one?

37
00:00:58.954 --> 00:01:02.125
(shouting and hollering)

38
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:03.211
When they play that song,

39
00:01:03.211 --> 00:01:04.997
"Jump Around, Jump Around" over again.

40
00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.072
(high-pitched sound effects)

41
00:01:07.072 --> 00:01:08.005
♫ Jump, jump!

42
00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:09.186
♫ Jump, jump!

43
00:01:09.186 --> 00:01:10.250
♫ Jump, jump!

44
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.083
♫ Jump!

45
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:12.520
Don't give them a section.

46
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.230
Many ancient sights here, Mount of Olives, right?

47
00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.253
Yes.
Dome of the Rock?

48
00:01:17.253 --> 00:01:18.277
Dome of the Rock.

49
00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.554
This must be a very ancient sight, it says, "Hyatt Hotel"

50
00:01:20.554 --> 00:01:22.403
this must be thousands of years old.

51
00:01:22.403 --> 00:01:25.810
This is the hotel where Joseph and Mary couldn't get a room?

52
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.964
Is that right, the Hyatt was completely booked?

53
00:01:28.964 --> 00:01:29.797
Probably.
And they gave it

54
00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:31.366
a terrible Yelp review.
(laughter)

55
00:01:31.366 --> 00:01:33.221
Donald Trump came to Jerusalem.

56
00:01:33.221 --> 00:01:34.054
Yeah.

57
00:01:34.054 --> 00:01:35.849
And he was very impressed with Jerusalem,

58
00:01:35.849 --> 00:01:39.304
he has a peace plan, a way to divide up the city

59
00:01:39.304 --> 00:01:42.107
that he thinks will bring great peace and harmony.

60
00:01:42.107 --> 00:01:43.707
Here's what he wants to do.

61
00:01:43.707 --> 00:01:46.160
Right over there, that's gonna be a Trump Hotel.

62
00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.149
Beautiful property, best in the world.

63
00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:51.021
That's gonna be a casino with a hummus fountain.

64
00:01:51.021 --> 00:01:53.255
This is a little evasion river for tourists,

65
00:01:53.255 --> 00:01:54.096
they can float around.

66
00:01:54.096 --> 00:01:57.421
And right here, everybody: Muslim, Christian, Jews

67
00:01:57.421 --> 00:02:01.333
will all live together in one condominium under the Force.

68
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:03.087
Do you think this could work?

69
00:02:03.087 --> 00:02:04.907
I love the river.

70
00:02:04.907 --> 00:02:07.234
And this, by the way, is real.

71
00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.245
His face is gonna be projected

72
00:02:09.245 --> 00:02:10.879
right over on that mountain there,

73
00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:13.748
it's gonna be 600ft tall, you okay with that?

74
00:02:13.748 --> 00:02:15.290
It's gonna go up in six months, and guess what?

75
00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.189
Mexico's gonna pay for it.
(laughter and applause)

76
00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:20.867
This is the Arab market in the old city,

77
00:02:20.867 --> 00:02:23.101
they have so many beautiful things to buy,

78
00:02:23.101 --> 00:02:25.010
haggling's a big thing here,

79
00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.237
and I wanted to learn more about it, so this is Benny.

80
00:02:27.237 --> 00:02:29.544
Benny, you understand the art of haggling,

81
00:02:29.544 --> 00:02:31.139
what's the first thing I need to know?

82
00:02:31.139 --> 00:02:34.181 line:15%
You need to tell that you saw exactly the same item

83
00:02:34.181 --> 00:02:38.348 line:15%
in the other shop, less than five euro, five dollar.

84
00:02:38.704 --> 00:02:40.469 line:15%
So wait, but what if that's a lie?

85
00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:41.723 line:15%
It's a lie.

86
00:02:41.723 --> 00:02:43.025 line:15%
What's another rule?

87
00:02:43.025 --> 00:02:45.847 line:15%
Now you say the quality, it's not so good.

88
00:02:45.847 --> 00:02:47.434 line:15%
"It's not so good"? That's insulting.

89
00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.464 line:15%
Any other tricks?

90
00:02:48.464 --> 00:02:50.360 line:15%
Yes, just to argue with them.

91
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.326 line:15%
Argue?

92
00:02:51.326 --> 00:02:54.056 line:15%
Until he will break up and he will take down the price.

93
00:02:54.056 --> 00:02:57.367
Hi, I'm interested in buying these products.

94
00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.863
The Jerusalem hat, how much is this?

95
00:02:59.863 --> 00:03:00.965 line:15%
Honest price: three dollars.

96
00:03:00.965 --> 00:03:02.775 line:15%
Three dollars?
Three dollars, ten sheckles.

97
00:03:02.775 --> 00:03:03.890 line:15%
That's bullshit.

98
00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:04.723 line:15%
Why?

99
00:03:04.723 --> 00:03:06.503 line:15%
I'm not gonna pay $3 for this hat.

100
00:03:06.503 --> 00:03:07.536 line:15%
Is it expensive?

101
00:03:07.536 --> 00:03:08.770
Three dollars, that's way too much.

102
00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:09.603 line:15%
Too much?

103
00:03:09.603 --> 00:03:10.436
Yeah, and guess what, I saw it

104
00:03:10.436 --> 00:03:12.421
at another market for much less.

105
00:03:12.421 --> 00:03:14.367 line:15%
Go ahead, go buy it wherever you like.

106
00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.494 line:15%
No, I don't wanna go to that market.

107
00:03:16.494 --> 00:03:18.992
I didn't like that market, it had a weird smell.

108
00:03:18.992 --> 00:03:19.903
This market I like.

109
00:03:19.903 --> 00:03:22.218
I'll buy it at this market, but not for $3.

110
00:03:22.218 --> 00:03:23.259
That's bullshit!

111
00:03:23.259 --> 00:03:24.534 line:15%
Why are you screaming?

112
00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.552
I don't know, I'm haggling with you.

113
00:03:26.552 --> 00:03:27.976 line:15%
Are you angry?

114
00:03:27.976 --> 00:03:29.675
Yes, about my childhood.

115
00:03:29.675 --> 00:03:30.687 line:15%
You wanna have coffee and tea,

116
00:03:30.687 --> 00:03:32.056 line:15%
then we talk about business?

117
00:03:32.056 --> 00:03:33.690
I would love to have some coffee with you,

118
00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:34.523 line:15%
that'd be very nice.

119
00:03:34.523 --> 00:03:35.799 line:15%
You like coffee with sugar or without sugar?

120
00:03:35.799 --> 00:03:37.226 line:15%
This is not the way haggling is supposed to go.

121
00:03:37.226 --> 00:03:38.348
(laughter and applause)

122
00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:41.129
How about this one, what's your price?

123
00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:42.679 line:15%
$150 I make it.

124
00:03:42.679 --> 00:03:43.892 line:15%
Hundred and fifty dollars?

125
00:03:43.892 --> 00:03:45.241 line:15%
Yes-
That's bullshit!

126
00:03:45.241 --> 00:03:47.406 line:15%
So what's not bullshit?

127
00:03:47.406 --> 00:03:48.878
$60 for this guitar.

128
00:03:48.878 --> 00:03:50.990 line:15%
No, it's too little, brother, it's too little.

129
00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.456
I'll give you...

130
00:03:52.456 --> 00:03:53.623
65?

131
00:03:53.623 --> 00:03:54.744 line:15%
No.

132
00:03:54.744 --> 00:03:55.834 line:15%
70?
No.

133
00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:56.981 line:15%
75?
No.

134
00:03:56.981 --> 00:03:58.283 line:15%
80?
No.

135
00:03:58.283 --> 00:03:59.444 line:15%
85.
No.

136
00:03:59.444 --> 00:04:00.452 line:15%
90.
No.

137
00:04:00.452 --> 00:04:01.514 line:15%
95.
No.

138
00:04:01.514 --> 00:04:02.515
How am I doing?

139
00:04:02.515 --> 00:04:04.263
(laughter)

140
00:04:04.263 --> 00:04:05.096
[Conan] How much for the camel?

141
00:04:05.096 --> 00:04:05.967 line:15%
- Ten dollars.

142
00:04:05.967 --> 00:04:06.909 line:15%
Ten dollars?

143
00:04:06.909 --> 00:04:08.073 line:15%
How much you want?

144
00:04:08.073 --> 00:04:08.906 line:15%
Ten dollars.

145
00:04:08.906 --> 00:04:09.856 line:15%
Ten dollars?

146
00:04:09.856 --> 00:04:10.739 line:15%
We will give you five dollars.

147
00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:11.729 line:15%
Five dollars?

148
00:04:11.729 --> 00:04:13.642 line:15%
Yes, to close.

149
00:04:13.642 --> 00:04:14.985 line:15%
No, no, for this one.

150
00:04:14.985 --> 00:04:17.068
(laughs)

151
00:04:18.764 --> 00:04:20.800
You're terrible at haggling.

152
00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.720
Of course, the most sacred sight of all of Old Jerusalem

153
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.882
is this Alabama Heart of Dixie Crimson Tide store.

154
00:04:27.882 --> 00:04:30.307
(laughter and applause)
Roll tide.

155
00:04:30.307 --> 00:04:33.557
(mellow Eastern music)

156
00:04:36.618 --> 00:04:39.688
I'm not touching you, my hands are above you

157
00:04:39.688 --> 00:04:41.261
and off to the side.

158
00:04:41.261 --> 00:04:42.094
Ah!

159
00:04:43.506 --> 00:04:44.516
Thank you very much.

160
00:04:44.516 --> 00:04:46.106
Nice, what is your name?

161
00:04:46.106 --> 00:04:47.085
David.
David?

162
00:04:47.085 --> 00:04:47.952
Yeah.

163
00:04:47.952 --> 00:04:49.873
Do you live here?
Yeah, I live here.

164
00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:50.956
This is beautiful, thank you.

165
00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:52.886 line:15%
It was very nice to meet you.
Maybe you come here

166
00:04:52.886 --> 00:04:55.196 line:15%
to drink coffee or something.

167
00:04:55.196 --> 00:04:56.586
We could do a coffee?

168
00:04:56.586 --> 00:04:58.086
At my apartment.

169
00:04:59.017 --> 00:05:00.019
Want me to come up to your apartment?

170
00:05:00.019 --> 00:05:00.852
I live here.

171
00:05:00.852 --> 00:05:04.256
If I'm done shooting maybe later on I can come by.

172
00:05:04.256 --> 00:05:05.842 line:15%
I don't believe you.

173
00:05:05.842 --> 00:05:07.362
You don't believe me?

174
00:05:07.362 --> 00:05:10.695
(laughter and applause)

175
00:05:13.485 --> 00:05:14.568
This is nice.

176
00:05:17.302 --> 00:05:19.442 line:15%
It's me.
Oh, it's you, oh good!

177
00:05:19.442 --> 00:05:22.267
(laughter)

178
00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.386
Tell me about yourself, David.

179
00:05:24.386 --> 00:05:25.969
I have five kids.

180
00:05:26.873 --> 00:05:28.509
You have five kids?

181
00:05:28.509 --> 00:05:29.342
Yeah.

182
00:05:31.668 --> 00:05:34.046
And 19 grandchildren.

183
00:05:34.046 --> 00:05:37.016
You have 19 grandchildren?
Yes, 19.

184
00:05:37.016 --> 00:05:39.201
Does your family know that you meet strangers

185
00:05:39.201 --> 00:05:43.368
on the street and invite them up to your house for coffee?

186
00:05:43.763 --> 00:05:45.733
Do they know about that?

187
00:05:45.733 --> 00:05:48.509
I worry about you, I don't want you doing that too much.

188
00:05:48.509 --> 00:05:50.430
Because I could be crazy, right?

189
00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.648
Look at me, I could be crazy.

190
00:05:52.648 --> 00:05:54.615 line:15%
No, you're beautiful.

191
00:05:54.615 --> 00:05:55.959 line:15%
(laughter and applause)

192
00:05:55.959 --> 00:05:58.692
I see,

193
00:05:58.692 --> 00:06:00.727
but I'm okay with it.

194
00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.244
Can I give you a gift?
No.

195
00:06:02.244 --> 00:06:03.466
Please, may I?
No.

196
00:06:03.466 --> 00:06:06.216
I think you're gonna like this.

197
00:06:08.411 --> 00:06:11.355
It's a yamaka, you like that?

198
00:06:11.355 --> 00:06:12.462
(laughter)

199
00:06:12.462 --> 00:06:13.295 line:15%
It's for you.

200
00:06:13.295 --> 00:06:14.583 line:15%
It's a nice memory.

201
00:06:14.583 --> 00:06:17.005 line:15%
It's a nice memory of our meeting.

202
00:06:17.005 --> 00:06:19.518
Those are very hard to come by

203
00:06:19.518 --> 00:06:21.251
because nobody really wants them.

204
00:06:21.251 --> 00:06:24.166
(laughter)

205
00:06:24.166 --> 00:06:26.245
Will you wear this ever?

206
00:06:26.245 --> 00:06:27.078
Yes!

207
00:06:28.274 --> 00:06:29.973
You look good.

208
00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:31.390
You're my friend.

209
00:06:32.843 --> 00:06:34.093 line:15%
And you also.

210
00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:41.187
You are the lowest energy human being I've ever met.

211
00:06:41.396 --> 00:06:43.574
Very little energy.

212
00:06:43.574 --> 00:06:44.629
Yes, of course.

213
00:06:44.629 --> 00:06:48.566
I think your heart has beat twice since I met you.

214
00:06:48.566 --> 00:06:50.656 line:15%
You artist, no?

215
00:06:50.656 --> 00:06:54.168 line:15%
Not really, no, I'm a comedian in America,

216
00:06:54.168 --> 00:06:56.393
I try to make people laugh.

217
00:06:56.393 --> 00:06:57.226
Yeah.

218
00:06:58.549 --> 00:07:01.714
I've been doing that for a long time.

219
00:07:01.714 --> 00:07:05.462
And as you can see, I'm very, very funny.

220
00:07:05.462 --> 00:07:08.503
(laughter and applause)

221
00:07:08.503 --> 00:07:09.981
This is something that I did.

222
00:07:09.981 --> 00:07:10.814
Wow.

223
00:07:12.304 --> 00:07:13.212 line:15%
Who is it?

224
00:07:13.212 --> 00:07:15.127
[Conan] That's me.

225
00:07:15.127 --> 00:07:17.127
(crows)

226
00:07:18.062 --> 00:07:19.430
I peck at you!

227
00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:20.379
I peck at your eyes!

228
00:07:20.379 --> 00:07:22.386
[Conan] You see my eye, yes.

229
00:07:22.386 --> 00:07:23.235
Will you still be my friend

230
00:07:23.235 --> 00:07:26.188
even though you know this is what I do?

231
00:07:26.188 --> 00:07:28.022
(crowing)

232
00:07:28.022 --> 00:07:28.997 line:15%
Wow.

233
00:07:28.997 --> 00:07:32.330 line:15%
(laughter and cheering)

